WEBVTT

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.020
Excuse me. Is this seat taken?

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.560
Oh, thank you.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.360
Oh, let me help you with this.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.800
Oh, thank you.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.000
Do you want to sit by the window?

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.020
No, no, no. I like the aisle seat better.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.430
Please, you sit by the window.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.420
My name is Stewart... Malcolm Stewart.

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:42.700
Pleased to meet you.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.620
I'm Elsa Tobin. How do you do?

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.640
Do you live in New York?

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.460
No, no. I'm from Florida.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:00.200
I am, too. But didn't you just get on?

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.590
No, no. I just changed my seat.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.080
A man next to me was smoking,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.620
and smoke really bothers me.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.000
Where are you from in Florida?

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.900
Titusville. It's near Orlando.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.660
Small world. I'm from Titusville, too.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.800
My husband and I live near Spaceport.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:26.360
I know that area.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.040
My house is only a few miles from Spaceport.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:33.120
Do you still live there?

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.200
Oh yes, yes. My husband's there now.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.840
He couldn't take time off to come to New York with me.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.060
Do you still live there?

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:48.840
No. I sold the house and the furniture,

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.260
put a few personal things in an old trunk,

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:56.280
and shipped it to my children in New York.

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.400
That's my destination.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:01:59.860
Are you married?

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.160
My wife died four years ago.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:12.460
I'm sorry. Really, I'm sorry.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.600
Lots of wonderful memories.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.140
We were married almost fifty years.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.960
Well, forty-seven, to be exact.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.710
John and I celebrate our fortieth anniversary next month.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.680
Oh, congratulations! That's nice.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.640
What does John do?

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.560
He's an aerospace engineer

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.280
and works for Orlando Aircraft Corporation.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.900
He started with them almost forty years ago.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.180
What do you do?

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:49.820
I just retired. Had my own company.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:55.310
A construction company. Roads, bridges, big stuff.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.160
But I just sold it and retired.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:05.970
Excuse me, ma'am. Ticket, please.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:11.880
Would you kindly hold these keys, please?

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.440
I have a ticket, I know.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.100
I was in the smoking section.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.610
It's OK, lady. Take your time.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.620
I'm sure it's in your purse, Mrs. Tobin.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.660
Oh, here it is.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:31.680
And here are your keys.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:32.740
Thank you.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.500
Do you have family in New York?

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:45.640
No, no. But I do have very close friends in New York City.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.220
We like to go to the theater together.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.400
Yes, indeed.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:57.000
A son and his wife and their three children--

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.360
my grandchildren.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:03:59.840
You must be excited.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.960
I can't wait, to see them!

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.420
Are you going to live with them?

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.420
Yes.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.700
Well... they want me to,

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.880
but it's too early to know for sure.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.380
I'm pretty independent.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:21.280
I tried to teach my kids the importance of independence

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.000
but I'm not sure I want to be alone.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:31.940
Some people don't mind being alone. I do.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.860
I understand. But tell me.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.680
Why did you stop working?

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:47.620
I retired because... I wanted to be with my family.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:51.140
I didn't want to be alone anymore!
